  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Iterating directly over a map (`for k in obj`) is not supported — see\n[Types](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/types.html#objects-maps).\n\n## Break and continue\n\n`continue` skips to the next iteration; `break` leaves the innermost loop:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "for i in 0..5 {\n    if i % 2 == 0 {\n        continue\n    }\n    print(i)\n}\n\nfor i in 0..10 {\n    if i == 3 {\n        break\n    }\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:119",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "1\n3\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-14",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Match\n\n`match` selects among arms by comparing a value to literal patterns, with `_` as\nthe wildcard. It is an **expression**: bind its result with `let`.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let v = 2\nlet word = match v {\n    1 => \"one\",\n    2 => \"two\",\n    _ => \"many\"\n}\nprint(word)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:145",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "two\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-16",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Supported patterns: integer, string and bool literals, `_`, and a bare\nidentifier that binds the scrutinee (`n => \"got \" + n`). Arm bodies can be an\nexpression or a `{ ... }` block whose last expression is the value:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-9",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let n = 5\nlet msg = match n {\n    0 => \"zero\",\n    other => \"got \" + other\n}\nprint(msg)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:164",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "got 5\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-18",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Current limitations (alpha):\n\n- **Not used as a statement.** `match v { 1 => print(\"one\"), _ => print(\"other\") }`\n  on its own fails at run time with `stack underflow`; the arms must produce\n  values and the result must be bound with `let` (or use `if` for side effects).\n- **`return match ...` returns `null`.** Bind first, then return:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn name(v) {\n    let r = match v {\n        0 => \"zero\",\n        _ => \"other\"\n    }\n    return r\n}\nprint(name(0))\nprint(name(3))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:185",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "zero\nother\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-20",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "- A `match` with no matching arm evaluates to `null` — there is no\n  exhaustiveness error.\n- No guards (`x if x > 3 => ...`) and no range patterns (`0..3 => ...`).\n\n(These are crush-ast gaps without a ticket yet; see `GAP-MATCH-STATEMENT` and\n`GAP-MATCH-RETURN` in the GUIDE-3 notes.)\n\n## Errors: `try` / `catch` / `throw`\n\n`throw` raises any value; `catch name { ... }` receives it. There is no\n`finally`, and the parenthesised form `catch (e)` is not accepted.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-11",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn divide(a, b) {\n    if b == 0 {\n        throw \"division by zero\"\n    }\n    return a / b\n}\n\ntry {\n    print(divide(4, 2))\n    print(divide(1, 0))\n    print(\"not reached\")\n} catch err {\n    print(\"Error: \" + err)\n}\nprint(\"done\")\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:215",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\nError: division by zero\ndone\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-22",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "A `throw` crosses function-call boundaries (fixed in crush-ast **CRUSH-126**),\n`catch` can rethrow, and thrown values can be any type:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "try {\n    try {\n        throw \"inner\"\n    } catch e {\n        throw \"re-\" + e\n    }\n} catch outer {\n    print(outer)\n}\n\ntry {\n    throw {\"code\": 7}\n} catch e {\n    print(e.code)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/control_flow.md:243",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "re-inner\n7\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-md-24",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "An uncaught `throw` ends the program with `[runtime] uncaught error: <value>`.\n\n### What `catch` does *not* catch\n\n`try`/`catch` handles values raised with `throw`. **Runtime faults from the VM or\na host capability are not catchable**: division by zero, an out-of-range array\nindex, a failing `fs.read`, or a polyglot block that raises all abort the\nprogram with a `[runtime]` error instead of reaching your `catch`.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-control-flow-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    try {\n        print(1 / 0)\n    } catch e {\n        print(\"caught\")\n    }\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
